        "reasoning": "The isentropic vortex test is a standard test case for evaluating the accuracy of numerical methods in fluid dynamics. In this test, a vortex is advected diagonally in a doubly periodic domain. The L2 density error is a measure of the difference between the numerical solution and the exact solution. Running this test in ERF on a 64x64 grid with (u_inf,v_inf)=(1,1) and reporting the L2 density error will provide insight into the accuracy of ERF's numerical methods. Baseline weights: configuration_complexity=0.100, development_activity=0.100, domain_models=0.100, grid_specifications=0.200, path_hierarchy=0.150, physics_parameters=0.300, resource_requirements=0.050.",
